<script>
import { url } from '@abide/abide'

import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Exchange from '#src/lib/Exchange.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/data/database',
        '/data/table',
        '/orchestration/job',
        '/data/fetch-and-handle',
        '/reactive/refresh',
        '/helpers/is-failed',
    ]}
>
    <Section title="Open the CRM's database once, in a server file">
        <p><a href={url('/data/database')}><code>database</code></a> comes from
            <code>@abide/abide/server</code>, so the opener lives in a <code>.server.ts</code>
            file and never reaches a browser. The first call opens <code>crm.sqlite</code> and runs
            each migration it has not run, in order. Every call after hands back the same
            <code>bun:sqlite</code> <code>Database</code>.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { database } from '@abide/abide/server'

            export const crmDatabase = database('crm', {
                migrations: [
                    \`CREATE TABLE targets (
                        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
                        target INTEGER NOT NULL,
                        setAt TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
                    )\`,
                    'CREATE TABLE digests (sentAt INTEGER NOT NULL)',
                ],
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Read the rows in a handler, and a page calls the handler">
        <p>A page reaches the rows through a handler declared with
            <a href={url('/handlers/rpc')}><code>GET</code></a>, which runs the query on the
            server and answers the rows as JSON.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { crmDatabase } from './lib/crmDatabase.server.ts'

            export default rpc(
                () =>
                    crmDatabase()
                        .query(
                            \`SELECT id, target, setAt FROM targets
                            ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 5\`,
                        )
                        .all() as { id: number; target: number; setAt: string }[],
                { description: 'Lists the targets the team has set, newest first.' },
            )
        `} />
        <p>The CRM's targets, asked when this page loaded. A server nobody has set a target on
            answers an empty list.</p>
        <Exchange path="/pipeline/listTargets" />
    </Section>

    <Section title="A write on the server changes nothing a page holds">
        <p>Write the row in a <a href={url('/handlers/rpc')}><code>POST</code></a>, then
            reload what read the table. The list a page holds is its last answer, and nothing
            tells the page a row was added until
            <a href={url('/reactive/refresh')}><code>refresh</code></a> asks again.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { reactive } from '@abide/abide'
            import listTargets from '../listTargets.server.ts'
            import setTarget from '../setTarget.server.ts'

            const targets = reactive.derived(() => listTargets())

            async function record() {
                await setTarget({ target: 600_000 })
                targets.refresh()
            }
            </script>

            <button onclick={record}>Set target</button>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Reload every value tagged with a table, whoever wrote the row">
        <p>A refresh after the CRM's own write misses a row the <code>sqlite3</code> shell or a
            second server commits. Name the table with
            <a href={url('/data/table')}><code>table</code></a>, and every <code>memo</code> whose
            <code>tags</code> name it loads again after any committed change.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { memo } from '@abide/abide'
            import { table } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { crmDatabase } from '../pipeline/lib/crmDatabase.server.ts'

            const latest = 'SELECT target FROM targets ORDER BY id DESC'

            table(crmDatabase, 'targets')
            export const target = memo(() => crmDatabase().query(latest).get(), {
                global: true,
                tags: ['targets'],
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Work on the records every weekday morning with a job">
        <p>A <a href={url('/orchestration/job')}><code>job</code></a> runs on the server, one run at a
            time, and nothing runs as the file loads. The CRM's digest goes out at eight on weekday
            mornings in New York, writes a row as it does, and keeps its status in the CRM's database,
            so a restart sends a morning it missed once and never twice.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { job, log, store } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { crmDatabase } from '../../pipeline/lib/crmDatabase.server.ts'
            import { DEALS } from '../../pipeline/lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export const digest = job({
                name: 'digest',
                cron: '0 8 * * 1-5',
                timeZone: 'America/New_York',
                run: async () => {
                    const leads = DEALS.filter((deal) => deal.stage === 'lead')
                    await Bun.sleep(300) // the mail going out
                    crmDatabase().run('INSERT INTO digests (sentAt) VALUES (?)', [
                        Date.now(),
                    ])
                    log.info(\`digest sent: \${leads.length} leads to follow up\`)
                },
                store: store.sqlite(crmDatabase, 'digest'),
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section title="A run that throws is the job's status, not a crash">
        <p>The error is logged under <code>job:digest</code> and kept as
            <code>lastError</code> until a run succeeds, and the schedule goes on. The CRM serves
            <code>digest.status</code> from a <code>GET</code>, so every page reads where the
            digest stands. <code>Job.run</code> in a <code>POST</code> sends the digest ahead of
            the schedule.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { digest } from './lib/digest.server.ts'

            export default rpc(digest.status, {
                description: 'When the follow-up digest last went out, and goes next.',
            })
        `} />
        <p>The digest's status, asked when this page loaded:</p>
        <Exchange path="/ops/getDigest" />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Fetch another service, on either side">
        <p><a href={url('/data/fetch-and-handle')}><code>fetchAndHandle</code></a> is
            <code>fetch</code> asked with a deadline and asked again after a 503, twice by default,
            its body read as its type says. Where the service still fails it rejects with a
            <code>FetchFailed</code>, and a handler that lets it reject refuses at 502.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { fetchAndHandle } from '@abide/abide'
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { registryOrigin } from './lib/registryOrigin.server.ts'

            type Registration = { founded: number; employees: number }

            export default rpc(
                ({ id }: { id: string }) =>
                    fetchAndHandle<Registration>(\`\${registryOrigin()}/companies/\${id}\`),
                { global: true, ttl: 60_000 },
            )
        `} />
        <p>The CRM's registry answers Hopper &amp; Co on every third ask, so the retries reach
            an answer. Asked when this page loaded:</p>
        <Exchange path="/companies/getRegistration?id=hopper-and-co" />
        <p>The registry never answers Langley Research, so the retries run out and the refusal
            is the answer:</p>
        <Exchange path="/companies/getRegistration?id=langley-research" />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Catch a FetchFailed to read why it gave up">
        <p>A refusal rejects, so catch it and narrow it with <code>fetchAndHandle.isError</code>.
            <code>as</code> reads the body as <code>'text'</code>, <code>'json'</code> or a
            <code>'blob'</code> whatever its type says.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { fetchAndHandle, log } from '@abide/abide'

            try {
                await fetchAndHandle('https://registry.example/filings/ada.txt', {
                    as: 'text',
                    timeout: 2_000,
                })
            } catch (failed) {
                if (!fetchAndHandle.isError(failed, 'FetchFailed')) throw failed
                log.warning('registry gave up', failed.data, failed.cause)
            }
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
